            "type": "mcq",
            "marks": 1,
            "question": "If $A$ and $B$ are two sets such that $n(A) = 115$, $n(B) = 326$, $n(A-B) = 47$, then $n(A \\cup B)$ is",
            "options": [
                "373",
                "165",
                "370",
                "394"
            ],
            "finalAnswer": "(a) 373",
            "solutionSteps": [
                "$n(A-B) = n(A) - n(A \\cap B) \\implies 47 = 115 - n(A \\cap B) \\implies n(A \\cap B) = 68$.",
                "$n(A \\cup B) = n(A) + n(B) - n(A \\cap B) = 115 + 326 - 68 = 441 - 68 = 373$."
            ]
        },
